Bug: a push in a project with -passN hangs the server

Any position request on a CU, in a project whose config has -passN sections, never
answers, with or without a preload. In the push's first pass processOptions lexes
-DPASS1 as a string, then singlePass starts the parse and the lexer loops on line 0
col 4, right after PASS1 in that string. The parser seems to read the define's
exhausted input instead of the source. The binary from e10dc05a hangs the same way.

test_multipass does not see it: -search does not parse the request file through
singlePass (server.c, "Not parsing input because of server operation TAG_SEARCH").

This test was written for a second question, which waits for the hang: singlePass
strips a preloaded file's references on every pass (the isPreloaded term), which
would throw away what the earlier passes added. Then pass1 would be missing below.
The expected output is written by hand, since the server has never answered here.
